  "label": "I'm about to end man",
  "description": "The phrase 'I'm about to end man' is a hyperbolic and apocalyptic metaphor. It is not literal but is used to convey a sense of impending, catastrophic destruction or extinction of humanity. This type of language is often used in dark humor, satire, or dystopian fiction to exaggerate the threat posed by a situation or entity. In this meme, it is used to amplify the perceived danger of rats, drawing on the historical association with plagues and disease.",
